# Athena-only mirror list — replaces Debian's Mirrors.masterlist.
#
# The installer's mirror-selection step (choose-mirror) offers ONLY this
# entry, so the operator gets a standard mirror step that lists our repo
# and never Debian.  choose-mirror validates the chosen mirror by fetching
#   http://<Site><Archive-http>/dists/<suite>/Release
# i.e. http://140.245.198.222/asgard/dists/thor/Release  (which exists).
#
# CAVEATS (see docs/plans/comp-01-choose-mirror-fork.md):
#   * host/path are hardcoded here, duplicating [Repo] AptSourceURL.
#     Follow-up: template these (@APT_SOURCE_HOST@/@APT_SOURCE_PATH@) and
#     substitute from AptSourceURL at fork-build time (one source of truth).
#   * the one-entry / country-grouping UX (and whether check-masterlist +
#     ./mirrorlist accept a country-less entry) needs build-time iteration.

Site: 140.245.198.222
Type: Push-Primary
Archive-architecture: amd64
Archive-http: /asgard/
